HTTP is the use of wifi to sned and recieve data through an API to a cloud for example, and I would choose it if I have a simple, connected to wifi system that updates data to a cloud.
MQTT, like HTTP REST, uses wifi, but the power consumption is less, and communication happpends through a brooker, where data is published to a topic, and user subscribes to this topic in order to collect data. I would choose it when i need real-time monitoring, many devices, or continuous sensor updates.
BLE (Blutooth) is the most commponly used communication type for short range and low power. This type works perfectly if we need to share data between close devices.
LoRa which stands for Long Range radio is an efficient long range data transmission communication type, where like FM or AM, data is transmitted through a ling range signal from the transmitter to the reciever, and I would use it if I want to transmit data from a temparature sensor in a huge farm.


